 "_README": "Which passes-register rows price each frontier configuration at the uniform discounted tier (PI ruling D19, amended 2026-10-04: every configuration's own tokens at one tier, flex, which equals batch on the rate card). Read by scripts/lib_frontier_cost.py (FrontierCoster.configuration_cost); design in planning/wp4b-frontier-cost-design-2026-10-04.md. Each entry: 'proposer', a list of {run_id, pool, passes}, costed as passes x the pool's mean pass (all passes when 'passes' is absent); 'verifier', either {'leg': {run_id, pool}} for a full run's own verifier leg, or {'unit_from': {run_id, pool}, 'candidates': N, 'candidates_source': {file, keys}} for a rung whose union of N candidates is costed at that leg's per-candidate unit (the convention of scripts/stride55_ladder.py), the count copied from the committed ladder named in candidates_source. A leg that is a floor in the register (a cleanup overwrote its main record) needs 'comparables': audited legs with an identical verifier configuration, nominated here so they can be reviewed; the library refuses a nominee that is itself a floor or differs in configuration. Nominations: stride A's union leg from stride B's (same campaign, corpus and day); FOURTH's 3.7 leg from ARM2's (the 3.7 verifier on the same 55-map corpus, same campaign); TM and IM from the four complete legs of the 55-map generalisation campaign they belong to.",
